    <GaugingStation location="Brigsley" name="Waithe Beck" number="29001">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Structure is able to contain all flows, gauging a rural, predominantly Chalk, catchment with significant artificial influences.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Theoretical rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Broad trapezoidal flume (1.83m wide at base) with theoretical rating confirmed to 0.9 cumecs. All recorded flows have been contained within the structure.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Groundwater abstraction near Grimsby and irrigation abstractions have significant effect on low flows. Also abstractions for PWS and industry. Runoff increased by effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly Chalk catchment with rural (mainly arable) land use.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">PGEI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Reasonable fit to gaugings." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Rating can not be validated beyond QMED." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
